{"title":"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is inscribed in a right isosceles triangle, and a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is circumscribed about the triangle. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a6fb22b042d9797c792decdeaa85932e30c32b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R/r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3e4134c78ef8d140483094609974189cab54b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 1+\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }2(2-\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"608\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1882135a1a49e9a11aad02c00fdb6cce17582b4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(0,1)--cycle); draw(circle((0.5,0.5),sqrt(2)/2)); draw(circle((1-sqrt(2)/2,1-sqrt(2)/2),1-sqrt(2)/2)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,1),NNW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1,0),SSE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0.5,0.5),NE); draw((0,0)--(0.5,0.5)); draw((1-sqrt(2)/2,1-sqrt(2)/2)--(0,1-sqrt(2)/2)); draw((1-sqrt(2)/2,1-sqrt(2)/2)--(1-sqrt(2)/2,0)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(1-sqrt(2)/2,0),S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(0,1-sqrt(2)/2),W); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,(1-sqrt(2)/2,1-sqrt(2)/2),NNW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Label the points as in the figure above. Let the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b094df35b928b83677e4e800c9ceef2ceb985e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=s$\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece324791b30cab9a41ad0f9a2ec0b01de79f112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=s\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. Since the circumradius of a right triangle is equal to half of the length of the hypotenuse, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/3512684c78274e56e8fdb8f2c4461428b1c471cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now to find the inradius. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8daca8128d69c2e5d98dd4f03b03577aaac5a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IFAE$\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> is a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5bf44b11089aa3d9fdf8959d494b201c4addb72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=R$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e26df512010d861e018d02e0af1eaa066485b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=AD=AI+ID=r\\sqrt{2}+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9926ad9356114882bdbf27fb52ac0703203203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{R}{\\sqrt{2}+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"91\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86bb269186d0279e52ab70456cd269bd83967a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{R}{r}=1+\\sqrt{2}, \\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME\" title=\"1974 AHSME\">1974 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1974 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1974 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1974\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1974 AHSME Pro